      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "summary": "What this topic covers.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "topic-map",
          "html": "<p>Every time you go online, your traffic passes through networks run by other people &mdash; the Wi-Fi you're on, your internet provider, and everyone in between. Each can see where your traffic is going, and anything that isn't encrypted. Network privacy is about limiting what those middlemen can see: HTTPS everywhere, private DNS, and tools like VPNs and Tor when you need more.</p>"
        }
      ]
